row(35, 18, 'MATERIAL', f'OR WITH A WOODEN INSTRUMENT OF THE HAND WHEREBY HE MAY DIE — THE THIRD INSTRUMENT; THE ROWS\' INDUCTION FROM THE THREE. {HP(35, 18, (("או", "בכלי", "עץ", "יד", "אשר", "ימות", "בו"), "OR with a WOODEN instrument of the hand whereby he may die — \'a wooden instrument\' one seat; \'whereby he may die\' with the masculine pronoun here and at 2 Kings 13:14 (Elisha\'s sickness \'whereof he died\' — the homograph of sense); the Sifrei 160:4 against Exodus 21:20\'s rod (computed)"), (("הכהו", "וימת", "רצח", "הוא", "מות", "יומת", "הרצח"), "he struck him and he died; he is a murderer — the murderer shall surely die: the formula\'s third seat; from the three the Hebrew 160:5 builds the induction (stone is not wood, wood not stone, neither iron — the common feature: it can kill) to \'anything\'; the English carries that induction at its 160:6 and gives 160:5 two sentences on the court-appointed avenger (the Hebrew\'s 160:7 tail) — the rows transposed between the files (computed on both)"))} → {AP(35, 18, (("או", "במאן", "דעא", "דמתנסב", "בידא"), "or with a vessel of wood that is taken in the hand"), (("דהיא", "כמסת", "די", "ימות", "ביה"), "which is sufficient that he die by it — the size clause supplied again"))}')
row(35, 19, 'MATERIAL', f'THE AVENGER OF BLOOD, HE SHALL PUT THE MURDERER TO DEATH; WHEN HE MEETS HIM HE SHALL PUT HIM TO DEATH — THE TRANSLATION PUTS THE COURT BEFORE HIS HAND. {HP(35, 19, (("גאל", "הדם", "הוא", "ימית", "את", "הרצח"), "THE AVENGER OF BLOOD, HE shall put the murderer to death — \'the avenger of blood\' ten Bible seats: this chapter\'s five verses (seven tokens), Deuteronomy 19:6, 12, Joshua 20:5, 9, and the woman of Tekoa\'s plea (2 Samuel 14:11); the redeem-root (Leviticus 25\'s redeemer) at six tokens here; the store glosses him \'be-the-next-of-kin\' (computed)"), (("בפגעו", "בו", "הוא", "ימיתנו"), "WHEN HE MEETS HIM, he shall put him to death — \'when he meets him\' two seats (19, 21); the Sifrei 160:5 (English) and 160:7 (both): the commandment is the avenger\'s, and one who has no avenger — the court appoints one (computed)"))} → {AP(35, 19, (("גאל", "דמא", "הוא", "יקטול", "ית", "קטולא"), "the avenger of blood, he shall kill the killer"), (("כד", "אתחיב", "ליה", "מן", "דינא", "הוא", "יקטלניה"), "WHEN HE HAS BEEN FOUND GUILTY BY THE COURT, he shall kill him — a clause of the translation\'s own at 19 and 21: the court\'s verdict before the avenger\'s hand, where the ink says \'when he meets him\'"))}')
row(35, 20, 'MATERIAL', f'IF IN HATRED HE THRUST HIM, OR THREW AT HIM IN LYING-IN-WAIT, AND HE DIED — THE WILFUL CASES WITHOUT AN INSTRUMENT; THE NOUN\'S TWO SEATS, EXODUS 21:13\'S VERB. {HP(35, 20, (("ואם", "בשנאה", "יהדפנו"), "AND IF IN HATRED HE THRUST HIM — \'in hatred\' two Bible seats (Ezekiel 23:29 the other); the thrust-root eleven Bible tokens, four the Torah\'s (Deuteronomy 6:19, 9:4 the nations thrust out; this and 35:22); the Sifrei 160:6: pushed from a roof — liable; into water or fire, or a dog or snake set on him — \'his judgment is given to Heaven\' (computed)"), (("או", "השליך", "עליו", "בצדיה", "וימת"), "or THREW at him IN LYING-IN-WAIT and he died — the noun\'s TWO Bible seats, both this chapter\'s (20, 22); its verb is EXODUS 21:13\'S SPEC (\'he lay not in wait\' — the place appointed for the unwitting) and David\'s (\'you hunt my soul\', 1 Samuel 24:12); the provisions-word wears the consonants at five other seats — the lemmas decide; \'threw at him\' two seats (20, 22) (computed)"))} → {AP(35, 20, (("ואם", "בסנאה", "דחהי"), "and if in hatred he pushed him"), (("או", "רמא", "עלוהי", "בכמנא", "וקטליה"), "or threw at him IN AMBUSH and killed him — the translation\'s ambush for the lying-in-wait"))}')
row(35, 21, 'MATERIAL', f'OR IN ENMITY HE STRUCK HIM WITH HIS HAND AND HE DIED: THE SMITER SHALL SURELY DIE, HE IS A MURDERER; THE AVENGER OF BLOOD PUTS HIM TO DEATH — THE SERPENT\'S WORD, THE QUARREL\'S SMITER. {HP(35, 21, (("או", "באיבה", "הכהו", "בידו", "וימת"), "OR IN ENMITY he struck him WITH HIS HAND and he died — THE ENMITY-NOUN\'S THREE TORAH SEATS: the serpent\'s (\'I will put enmity between you and the woman\', Genesis 3:15) and this chapter\'s two (21, 22), Ezekiel\'s two the Bible\'s others; \'struck him with his hand\' one seat; the Sifrei 160:7: crushed, strangled, kicked, trampled — \'with his hand\', in any manner (computed)"), (("מות", "יומת", "המכה", "רצח", "הוא"), "THE SMITER shall surely die, he is a murderer — the smiter as the participle with the article: the quarrel\'s striker (Exodus 21:19), Hadad who smote Midian (Genesis 36:35), David\'s plea (2 Samuel 24:17) and this chapter\'s two (21, 24); the same consonants are THE SMITTEN WOMAN at 25:14, 15, 18 (the passive by the morphology) and \'the blow\' in Samuel and Kings; \'struck him\' five Torah seats — this chapter\'s four and Deuteronomy 21:1\'s \'it is not known who struck him\' (computed)"), (("גאל", "הדם", "ימית", "את", "הרצח", "בפגעו", "בו"), "the avenger of blood shall put the murderer to death when he meets him — the Sifrei 160:7: why again? for one who has no avenger"))} → {AP(35, 21, (("או", "בדבבו", "מחהי", "בידיה", "וקטליה"), "or in enmity he struck him with his hand and killed him"), (("אתקטלא", "יתקטל", "מחיא", "קטולא", "הוא"), "the smiter shall surely be killed; he is a killer"), (("כד", "אתחיב", "ליה", "מן", "דינא"), "when he has been found guilty by the court — the court supplied a second time"))}')
row(35, 22, 'MATERIAL', f'BUT IF SUDDENLY, WITHOUT ENMITY, HE THRUST HIM, OR THREW ANY INSTRUMENT AT HIM WITHOUT LYING-IN-WAIT — THE UNWITTING CASES, THE WILFUL ONES\' MIRROR; THE NAZIRITE\'S "SUDDENLY". {HP(35, 22, (("ואם", "בפתע", "בלא", "איבה", "הדפו"), "AND IF SUDDENLY, WITHOUT ENMITY, he thrust him — \'suddenly\' two Bible seats, both this book\'s: the nazirite\'s \'if one die by him very suddenly\' (6:9) and this; \'without enmity\' one seat; the thrust-verb\'s second seat, 35:20\'s mirror; the Sifrei 160:8 \'to exclude the unwitting\' (computed)"), (("או", "השליך", "עליו", "כל", "כלי", "בלא", "צדיה"), "or threw at him ANY INSTRUMENT WITHOUT LYING-IN-WAIT — 35:20\'s \'in lying-in-wait\' negated, the noun\'s second seat; \'any instrument\' the tabernacle\'s phrase (eighteen Torah seats) (computed)"))} → {AP(35, 22, (("ואם", "בתכף", "בלא", "דבבו", "דחהי"), "and if suddenly, without enmity, he pushed him — the translation\'s \'suddenly\' at the nazirite\'s (6:9), Miriam\'s (12:4) and this"), (("או", "רמא", "עלוהי", "כל", "מאן", "בלא", "כמן"), "or threw at him any vessel without ambush"))}')
row(35, 23, 'MATERIAL', f'OR WITH ANY STONE WHEREBY HE MAY DIE, WITHOUT SEEING, AND DROPPED IT ON HIM AND HE DIED, AND HE WAS NOT HIS ENEMY NOR SOUGHT HIS HARM — THE BLIND MAN\'S CLAUSE, THE JUDGES\' DISQUALIFICATION. {HP(35, 23, (("או", "בכל", "אבן", "אשר", "ימות", "בה"), "or with any stone whereby he may die — the size clause a third time"), (("בלא", "ראות", "ויפל", "עליו", "וימת"), "WITHOUT SEEING, and he dropped it on him and he died — one seat each; the Sifrei 160:8: \'without seeing\' includes the blind man and the night-thrower, R. Yehudah excludes the blind; Issi ben Akiva: his stringency his leniency — neither death nor exile can be imposed (computed)"), (("והוא", "לא", "אויב", "לו", "ולא", "מבקש", "רעתו"), "AND HE WAS NOT HIS ENEMY NOR SEEKING HIS HARM — one seat each; the Sifrei 160:8 reads the clause with 35:24\'s judging: haters and kin disqualified from judging, then from witnessing by the a-fortiori (computed)"))} → {AP(35, 23, (("או", "בכל", "אבנא", "דהיא", "כמסת", "די", "ימות"), "or with any stone which is sufficient that he die"), (("בלא", "חזי", "ורמא", "עלוהי", "וקטליה"), "without seeing, and threw it on him and killed him"), (("והוא", "לא", "סני", "ליה", "ולא", "תבע", "בישתיה"), "and he did not hate him and did not seek his harm"))}')
row(35, 24, 'MATERIAL', f'THE CONGREGATION SHALL JUDGE BETWEEN THE SMITER AND THE AVENGER OF BLOOD BY THESE JUDGMENTS — THE COURT OF TWENTY-THREE FROM THE CONGREGATION-TOKENS. {HP(35, 24, (("ושפטו", "העדה", "בין", "המכה", "ובין", "גאל", "הדם"), "AND THE CONGREGATION SHALL JUDGE between the smiter and the avenger of blood — one seat; the congregation-token four times in the chapter (12, 24, 25, 25): the Sifrei 160:8\'s ten who judge and ten who deliver, three added (\'a court is not even\') — twenty-three, its Hebrew; the English says THIRTY and cites \'[27]\' for the tokens (computed)"), (("על", "המשפטים", "האלה"), "BY THESE JUDGMENTS — the phrase here and Deuteronomy 7:12; the Sifrei: all capital cases, the stranger too, by twenty-three — and not monetary cases (Exodus 22:8\'s \'unto the judges\') (computed)"))} → {AP(35, 24, (("וידונון", "כנשתא", "בין", "מחיא", "ובין", "גאל", "דמא"), "and the assembly shall judge between the smiter and the avenger of blood"), (("על", "דיניא", "האלין"), "by these judgments"))}')
row(35, 25, 'MATERIAL', f'THE CONGREGATION SHALL DELIVER THE SLAYER FROM THE AVENGER, RETURN HIM TO HIS CITY OF REFUGE, AND HE SHALL DWELL IN IT UNTIL THE DEATH OF THE HIGH PRIEST ANOINTED WITH THE HOLY OIL — THE TERM, THE HIGH PRIEST WRITTEN DEFECTIVE, THE TRANSLATION DELIVERING WITH THE REFUGE-ROOT. {HP(35, 25, (("והצילו", "העדה", "את", "הרצח", "מיד", "גאל", "הדם"), "AND THE CONGREGATION SHALL DELIVER the slayer from the hand of the avenger of blood — one seat; the Sifrei 160:9: all who kill, unwitting or wilful, go first to the cities, the court sends and brings them (computed)"), (("והשיבו", "אתו", "העדה"), "and the congregation shall return him — one seat"), (("אל", "עיר", "מקלטו", "אשר", "נס", "שמה"), "to his city of refuge where he fled — \'he fled there\' the perfect\'s one seat; \'his city of refuge\' five tokens (25, 26, 27, 28, 32) (computed)"), (("וישב", "בה", "עד", "מות", "הכהן", "הגדל"), "AND HE SHALL DWELL IN IT UNTIL THE DEATH OF THE HIGH PRIEST — the term\'s seats 35:25, 28 and Joshua 20:6 quoting it PLENE; THE HIGH PRIEST WRITTEN DEFECTIVE ONLY HERE (35:25, 28 twice — the Bible\'s three tokens), plene at sixteen seats and \'and the high priest\' at Leviticus 21:10 (the definition by the oil poured on his head) and 2 Kings 12:11; the Sifrei 160:9 — R. Meir: the murderer shortens days, the high priest lengthens them; Rebbi: the one defiles the land, the other brings the Presence to rest (computed)"), (("אשר", "משח", "אתו", "בשמן", "הקדש"), "WHO WAS ANOINTED WITH THE HOLY OIL — the phrase\'s one seat; \'the anointing oil\' the tabernacle\'s nine; the exam\'s three high priests (Makkot 11a) (computed)"))} → {AP(35, 25, (("וישזבון", "כנשתא", "ית", "קטולא"), "AND THE ASSEMBLY SHALL GIVE REFUGE TO the killer — the translation renders \'deliver\' with the refuge-root itself: twelve refuge-tokens in the chapter for the Hebrew\'s eleven"), (("ויתב", "בה", "עד", "דימות", "כהנא", "רבא"), "and he shall dwell in it until the GREAT priest dies — \'great\' the word of 34\'s princes and the great sea"), (("די", "רבי", "יתיה", "במשח", "קודשא"), "whom he anointed with the oil of holiness — the anointing-verb\'s one seat in the book"))}')
row(35, 26, 'MATERIAL', f'BUT IF THE SLAYER GOING OUT GOES OUT BEYOND THE BORDER OF HIS CITY OF REFUGE — THE DOUBLED INFINITIVE OF JACOB\'S GOING OUT; THE BORDER GIVEN THE SABBATH LIMIT\'S WORD. {HP(35, 26, (("ואם", "יצא", "יצא", "הרצח"), "AND IF THE SLAYER GOING OUT GOES OUT — the doubled infinitive\'s two Bible seats: Jacob\'s \'had scarcely gone out\' from Isaac (Genesis 27:30) and this; the chapter\'s sixth doubled infinitive after the five \'surely die\'; the Sifrei 160:10, R. Elazar ben Azariah: one step outside forfeits the soul under the lesser measure — how much more the greater (computed)"), (("את", "גבול", "עיר", "מקלטו", "אשר", "ינוס", "שמה"), "the BORDER of his city of refuge where he flees — \'the border of his city of refuge\' one seat; \'he shall flee there\' three: EXODUS 21:13 (the spec: \'a place to which he shall flee\'), Deuteronomy 19:4 and this; the store glosses the going out \'bring-forth\' (computed)"))} → {AP(35, 26, (("ואם", "מפק", "יפוק", "קטולא"), "and if the killer going out goes out"), (("ית", "תחום", "קרית", "שזבותיה"), "the LIMIT of his city of refuge — the Sabbath-limit\'s word (techum, the two thousand cubits of 35:5 in the exam\'s law), the word the translation gave the borders of 34 and Sihon\'s (21:13)"))}')
row(35, 27, 'MATERIAL', f'THE AVENGER FINDS HIM OUTSIDE THE BORDER AND MURDERS THE SLAYER — HE HAS NO BLOOD: THE BURGLAR\'S ACQUITTAL AT ITS SECOND SEAT, THE ONE ROOT FOR FOUR AGENTS. {HP(35, 27, (("ומצא", "אתו", "גאל", "הדם", "מחוץ", "לגבול"), "and the avenger of blood finds him OUTSIDE THE BORDER of his city of refuge — one seat each; the Sifrei 160:10 \'any man\' (computed)"), (("ורצח", "גאל", "הדם", "את", "הרצח"), "AND THE AVENGER OF BLOOD MURDERS THE SLAYER — the murder-root as the avenger\'s own act: the chapter\'s twenty tokens of one root name the murderer, the manslayer, the avenger\'s kill (here) and the court\'s execution (35:30) — Hosea 4:2\'s the verb\'s only other seat in this form (computed)"), (("אין", "לו", "דם"), "HE HAS NO BLOOD — THE BURGLAR\'S CLAUSE (Exodus 22:1 \'there is no blood for him\', the plural; 22:2 \'he has blood\') at its second seat, the singular: the acquittal formula\'s two Torah seats, the householder\'s and the avenger\'s; the Sifrei 160:1 reads this clause against 35:12 — not before the court (computed)"))} → {AP(35, 27, (("מברא", "לתחום", "קרית", "שזבותיה"), "outside the limit of his city of refuge"), (("ויקטול", "גאל", "דמא", "ית", "קטולא"), "and the avenger of blood kills the killer"), (("לית", "ליה", "דמא"), "he has no blood — the translation keeps the ink\'s bare acquittal"))}')
row(35, 28, 'MATERIAL', f'FOR IN HIS CITY OF REFUGE HE SHALL DWELL UNTIL THE DEATH OF THE HIGH PRIEST, AND AFTER THE DEATH OF THE HIGH PRIEST THE SLAYER RETURNS TO THE LAND OF HIS POSSESSION — THE TERM STATED TWICE, JOSHUA ADDING THE HOUSE. {HP(35, 28, (("כי", "בעיר", "מקלטו", "ישב", "עד", "מות", "הכהן"), "FOR in his city of refuge he shall dwell until the death of the priest — \'for\' the case\'s reason-clause; the high priest defective again, twice in the verse (computed)"), (("ואחרי", "מות", "הכהן", "הגדל", "ישוב", "הרצח"), "and after the death of the HIGH PRIEST the slayer shall return — the clause one seat; the Sifrei 160:10: a Levite exiled from city to city; the returner not to his office (R. Yehudah), even to it (R. Meir) (computed)"), (("אל", "ארץ", "אחזתו"), "to THE LAND OF HIS POSSESSION — the phrase\'s one seat (the family six: Leviticus 14:34, 25:24, Joshua 22:4, 9, 19); JOSHUA 20:6 ADDS \'and come to his city and to his house\' (computed)"))} → {AP(35, 28, (("ארי", "בקרית", "שזבותיה", "יתב"), "for in his city of refuge he shall dwell"), (("ובתר", "דימות", "כהנא", "רבא", "יתוב", "קטולא"), "and after the great priest dies the killer shall return"), (("לארע", "אחסנתיה"), "to the land of his inheritance"))}')
row(35, 29, 'MATERIAL', f'THESE SHALL BE FOR YOU A STATUTE OF JUDGMENT FOR YOUR GENERATIONS IN ALL YOUR DWELLINGS — THE DAUGHTERS\' PHRASE, THE BLOOD BAN\'S FORMULA. {HP(35, 29, (("והיו", "אלה", "לכם", "לחקת", "משפט"), "AND THESE SHALL BE FOR YOU A STATUTE OF JUDGMENT — the phrase\'s two seats in the Bible: THE DAUGHTERS\' INHERITANCE (27:11) and this; the Sifrei 134:3 and 161:1 read each \'that the matter obtain for the generations\'; the translation \'a decree of judgment\' at both (computed)"), (("לדרתיכם", "בכל", "מושבתיכם"), "FOR YOUR GENERATIONS IN ALL YOUR DWELLINGS — LEVITICUS 3:17\'s formula, THE BLOOD BAN\'S (\'you shall eat no fat and no blood\'), at its second seat; \'in all your dwellings\' six seats (Exodus 12:20\'s leaven, Leviticus 3:17, 7:26 the blood again, 23:3, 21, this); the Sifrei 161:1: \'in the land and outside the land\' — the capital court everywhere (computed)"))} → {AP(35, 29, (("ויהון", "אלין", "לכון", "לגזרת", "דין"), "and these shall be for you a decree of judgment — the same two Aramaic words at 27:11"), (("לדריכון", "בכל", "מותבניכון"), "for your generations in all your dwellings"))}')
row(35, 30, 'MATERIAL', f'WHOEVER SMITES A SOUL, BY THE MOUTH OF WITNESSES SHALL THE MURDERER BE SLAIN; ONE WITNESS SHALL NOT TESTIFY AGAINST A PERSON TO DIE — THE SIXTH AND THE NINTH COMMANDMENTS\' VERBS IN ONE VERSE, THE HOMOGRAPH "UNTIL / WITNESS". {HP(35, 30, (("כל", "מכה", "נפש", "לפי", "עדים"), "WHOEVER SMITES A SOUL, BY THE MOUTH OF WITNESSES — the smiter-phrase\'s third seat in the chapter"), (("ירצח", "את", "הרצח"), "SHALL HE SLAY THE MURDERER — \'by the mouth of witnesses\' one seat, the bare plural without a number (Deuteronomy says \'two witnesses or three\', 17:6, 19:15); the murder-root for the court\'s execution — the sixth commandment\'s root (Exodus 20:13; Deuteronomy 5:17); the Sifrei 161:1: only in court and by witnesses (R. Yoshiyah, R. Yonatan) (computed)"), (("ועד", "אחד", "לא", "יענה", "בנפש", "למות"), "AND ONE WITNESS SHALL NOT TESTIFY against a person to die — \'and one witness\' one seat; \'ONE WITNESS\' A HOMOGRAPH: the consonants say \'not even one\' of Egypt\'s cattle (Exodus 9:7) and of the drowned (14:28), \'until one\' at Judges 4:16 and 2 Samuel 17:22, \'one witness\' at Deuteronomy 17:6, 19:15 — the lemmas decide; inside the chapter the same consonants are \'UNTIL\' four times (12, 25, 28, 32 — the fugitive\'s term) and \'witness\' twice here; \'SHALL NOT TESTIFY\' IS THE NINTH COMMANDMENT\'S VERB (\'you shall not answer against your neighbor a false witness\', Exodus 20:16; Deuteronomy 5:20; 19:18) — the verse carries the two commandments\' verbs; the store glosses the verb \'eye\'; the Sifrei 161:1: he may testify for acquittal, one witness obliges an oath, and the prototype — \'witness\' means two unless \'one\' is written (computed)"))} → {AP(35, 30, (("לפום", "סהדין", "יקטול", "ית", "קטולא"), "by the mouth of witnesses he shall kill the killer"), (("וסהיד", "חד", "לא", "יסהד", "באנש", "למקטל"), "and one witness shall not testify against a man to be killed — the translation\'s witness-verb"))} The register gate reads the verse\'s one as a measure — green, nothing to declare (computed).')
row(35, 31, 'MATERIAL', f'YOU SHALL NOT TAKE RANSOM FOR THE LIFE OF A MURDERER WHO IS WICKED TO DIE; HE SHALL SURELY DIE — THE GORING OX\'S RANSOM REFUSED, THE ROOT OF THE ATONEMENT. {HP(35, 31, (("ולא", "תקחו", "כפר", "לנפש", "רצח"), "AND YOU SHALL NOT TAKE RANSOM for the life of a murderer — the ransom-noun\'s four Torah seats: THE GORING OX\'S (Exodus 21:30 \'if a ransom be laid on him\'), THE HALF-SHEKEL\'S (\'a ransom for his soul\', Exodus 30:12) and this chapter\'s two; the Sifrei 161:1 sets the ox against the murderer: death at Heaven\'s hand is ransomed, death by the court is not; \'for the life of a murderer\' one seat; the store glosses the ransom \'cover\' (computed)"), (("אשר", "הוא", "רשע", "למות", "כי", "מות", "יומת"), "WHO IS WICKED TO DIE; FOR HE SHALL SURELY DIE — \'wicked to die\' one seat (Deuteronomy 25:2\'s \'the wicked one deserving stripes\' the kin; \'a son of death\' Saul\'s and David\'s); \'for he shall surely die\' with \'for\' one seat — the formula\'s fifth in the chapter; the Sifrei\'s R. Yoshiyah and R. Yonatan on one going out to be executed: until his verdict is finished, liable; after, exempt (computed)"))} → {AP(35, 31, (("ולא", "תקבלון", "ממון", "על", "אנש", "קטול"), "and you shall not receive MONEY for a man, a killer — the translation\'s money for the ransom, the word\'s only two seats in the book (31, 32); the killer bare, without the article, once"), (("די", "הוא", "חיב", "למקטל"), "who is GUILTY to be killed — \'guilty\' for \'wicked\'"))}')
row(35, 32, 'MATERIAL', f'YOU SHALL NOT TAKE RANSOM FOR ONE WHO FLED TO HIS CITY OF REFUGE, TO RETURN TO DWELL IN THE LAND UNTIL THE DEATH OF THE PRIEST — THE FUGITIVE\'S RANSOM REFUSED TOO; "THE PRIEST" WITHOUT "GREAT". {HP(35, 32, (("ולא", "תקחו", "כפר", "לנוס", "אל", "עיר", "מקלטו"), "AND YOU SHALL NOT TAKE RANSOM for one who fled to his city of refuge — the second refusal; the Sifrei 161:2: the wilful killer who would pay and be exiled instead (computed)"), (("לשוב", "לשבת", "בארץ", "עד", "מות", "הכהן"), "to return to dwell in the land UNTIL THE DEATH OF THE PRIEST — \'to return to dwell in the land\' one seat; the term\'s one seat WITHOUT \'great\' (35:25, 28 and Joshua 20:6 say \'the high priest\') (computed)"))} → {AP(35, 32, (("ולא", "תקבלון", "ממון", "למערוק", "לקרית", "שזבותיה"), "and you shall not receive money for fleeing to his city of refuge"), (("למתוב", "למתב", "בארעא", "עד", "דימות", "כהנא"), "to return to dwell in the land until the priest dies"))}')
row(35, 33, 'MATERIAL', f'YOU SHALL NOT POLLUTE THE LAND, FOR THE BLOOD POLLUTES THE LAND, AND FOR THE LAND NO ATONEMENT IS MADE FOR THE BLOOD SHED IN IT EXCEPT BY THE BLOOD OF HIM WHO SHED IT — THE POLLUTE-ROOT\'S ONLY TORAH SEAT, PSALM 106\'S ECHO, THE RANSOM\'S ROOT A THIRD TIME, THE HEIFER\'S OTHER PASSIVE. {HP(35, 33, (("ולא", "תחניפו", "את", "הארץ", "אשר", "אתם", "בה"), "AND YOU SHALL NOT POLLUTE THE LAND in which you are — the pollute-root\'s eleven Bible tokens: THE TORAH\'S ONLY SEAT IS THIS VERSE (two tokens, the causative), then Jeremiah\'s land polluted by harlotry (3:1, 2, 9), Isaiah 24:5, Micah 4:11, Daniel 11:32, Jeremiah 23:11 — and PSALM 106:38 \'and the land was polluted with blood\', this verse\'s verb with its blood; the Sifrei 161:3: an exhortation against the flatterers (the root\'s other sense), or \'do not cause the land to flatter you\'; the store glosses it \'soil\' (computed)"), (("כי", "הדם", "הוא", "יחניף", "את", "הארץ"), "FOR THE BLOOD, IT POLLUTES THE LAND — R. Yoshiyah\'s notarikon (the word split in two): \'it rests wrath\' — a move to name (computed on the shelf\'s bytes)"), (("ולארץ", "לא", "יכפר", "לדם", "אשר", "שפך", "בה"), "AND FOR THE LAND NO ATONEMENT CAN BE MADE for the blood shed in it — the passive (pual) one seat: the root of the RANSOM three times in the chapter (\'ransom\' 31, 32; \'be atoned\' 33) — no ransom for the murderer, none for the fugitive, no atonement for the land; the Sifrei 161:3: if the heifer\'s neck was broken and then the slayer found — no atonement (Deuteronomy 21:8\'s other passive \'and the blood shall be atoned for them\' the contrast) (computed)"), (("כי", "אם", "בדם", "שפכו"), "EXCEPT BY THE BLOOD OF HIM WHO SHED IT — Genesis 9:6\'s \'whoso sheds man\'s blood, by man shall his blood be shed\'; the Sifrei: bloodshed defiles the land and removes the Presence, and for it the Temple was destroyed (computed)"))} → {AP(35, 33, (("ולא", "תחיבון", "ית", "ארעא"), "and you shall not make the land GUILTY — the translation\'s guilt for the pollution"), (("ולארעא", "לא", "מתכפר", "על", "דם", "זכאי"), "and for the land there is no atonement for INNOCENT BLOOD — \'innocent\' SUPPLIED, the word\'s one seat in the book"), (("אלהן", "בדם", "אשדיה"), "except by the blood of him who shed it"))}')
row(35, 34, 'MATERIAL', f'YOU SHALL NOT DEFILE THE LAND IN WHICH YOU DWELL, IN WHOSE MIDST I DWELL, FOR I THE LORD DWELL IN THE MIDST OF THE CHILDREN OF ISRAEL — THE BOOK\'S INCLUSIO WITH 5:3, THE PRESENCE SUPPLIED, THE LAST WORDS OF THE LAW IN NUMBERS. {HP(35, 34, (("ולא", "תטמא", "את", "הארץ", "אשר", "אתם", "ישבים"), "AND YOU SHALL NOT DEFILE THE LAND in which you dwell — one seat; Leviticus 18:25, 27\'s \'and the land was defiled\' (the forbidden unions) the kin: the two defilers of the land, the unions and the blood (computed)"), (("בה", "אשר", "אני", "שכן", "בתוכה"), "IN WHOSE MIDST I DWELL — THE BOOK\'S INCLUSIO: 5:3 \'their camp in whose midst I dwell\' (the first law after the census) and this (the last law-chapter\'s close) are the Torah\'s two seats of \'I dwell in the midst\'; the Sifrei 1:7 and 161:5 read each by the other — \'beloved are Israel: even when unclean, the Presence among them\' (computed)"), (("כי", "אני", "יהוה", "שכן", "בתוך", "בני", "ישראל"), "FOR I THE LORD DWELL IN THE MIDST OF THE CHILDREN OF ISRAEL — one seat; Exodus 29:45-46\'s promise (\'I will dwell in the midst of the children of Israel\'; 25:8), 1 Kings 6:13 and Zechariah 8:3 its runs; the Sifrei 161:5, R. Natan: wherever exiled, the Presence with them — Egypt, Babylon, Elam, Edom — and returns WITH them (Deuteronomy 30:3\'s verb read in the simple stem); Rebbi\'s king with his son; the Hebrew\'s colophon after it: the book of Numbers is completed (computed on the export)"))} → {AP(35, 34, (("ולא", "תסאבון", "ית", "ארעא"), "and you shall not defile the land"), (("די", "שכינתי", "שריא", "בגוה"), "in which MY PRESENCE dwells — the Presence supplied, the word\'s one seat in the book (5:3\'s form \'my Presence dwells among them\')"), (("ארי", "אנא", "יי", "דשכנתי", "שריא", "בגו", "בני"), "for I am the LORD whose Presence dwells among the children of Israel"))}')
